      {
       "@type": "Review",
       "reviewRating": {
        "@type": "Rating",
        "ratingValue": "5"
       },
       "reviewBody": "Wonderful!!!  My husband and I love this recipe. I used the white mushrooms. May try others next time.  I KNOW I will be making again.",
       "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Cindy S"
       },
       "datePublished": "2019-04-01"
      },
      {
       "@type": "Review",
       "reviewRating": {
        "@type": "Rating",
        "ratingValue": "5"
       },
       "reviewBody": "I made this tonight and holy cow is it good!  So creamy and mushroomy.  I had 1/2 &amp; 1/2 on hand so that is what I used and I also sautéed shallots with the shrooms and garlic. It was a really nice additions!  I’m having it over pasta tonight, but the viewers mentioning pouring it over toast makes me look forward to breakfast!  I’m going to scramble an egg for the toast and smother it is fungi goodness.  Bon a petit!",
       "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "KKay"
       },
       "datePublished": "2018-07-03"
      },
      {
       "@type": "Review",
       "reviewRating": {
        "@type": "Rating",
        "ratingValue": "5"
       },
       "reviewBody": "I sauteed fresh sliced mushrooms with fresh garlic, in a olive oil/sea salt  butter blend with added extra virgin olive oil. I then combined half and half with Kraft grated parmesan  cheese and sauteed till blended and thickened . Inspired by another commenter, I spread the mushroom concoction on toasted honey wheat bread.  This dish was easy, filling and delicious. Can't wait to make again and serve with pasta and some kind of meat.",
